sentences.text:
5. In light of these considerations, this Court issues the following order:
ORDER (i) The appeal filed by the insurance company is allowed in part;
(ii) The judgment and award passed by the Tribunal in MVC.No.191/2016 is hereby modified to align with the findings of this Court;
Cholamandalam M.S. General Insurance ... vs Chandrakala And Ors on 8 November, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/150752876/
3 (iii) The appellant, namely the insurance company, is directed to satisfy the awarded compensation by depositing the compensation amount, inclusive of the interest rate specified by the Tribunal, without further delay;
(iv) The insurance company is granted liberty to recover the entire compensation amount, post-payment, from the owner of the offending vehicle;
NC: 2024:KHC-K:8293 (v) Any amounts already deposited with the Court shall be remitted to the Tribunal immediately to facilitate the disbursement process.
Sd/-
(SACHIN SHANKAR MAGADUM) JUDGE CA Cholamandalam M.S. General Insurance ... vs Chandrakala And Ors on 8 November, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/150752876/
